<title>SPAIN: Spain unaware of deal to delay EMU entry.</title>
<headline>Spain unaware of deal to delay EMU entry.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-02-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spanish Economy Secretary Cristobal Montoro said on Wednesday he knew of no deal to delay Spain or Italy's entry to European Economic and Monetary Union (EMU).</p>
<p>&quot;Absolutely not&quot;, said Montoro, when asked whether he knew of such a plan.</p>
<p>A report in the Financial Times today said Italy will be offered entry in to the single currency in 2000 or 2001, and the plan may be extended to Spain and Portugal.  </p>
<p>Speaking after a parliamentary committee meeting, Montoro added: &quot;Delays in the established EMU timetable would not suit Spain&quot; he added.</p>
<p>-- Madrid newsroom +341 585 2160</p>
